LMA SoulX-Podcast acoustic research module (not registered in the APK)

The offline Python graph wrappers adapt the complete acoustic modules in
Soul-AILab/SoulX-Podcast, Apache-2.0, at the revision and file hashes in
third_party/soulx-acoustic-source-lock.json. The relevant upstream credits
include Soul-AILab contributors and Alibaba Inc. LMA adaptations:
Copyright 2026 LMA contributors, Apache-2.0. The license is supplied here
as LICENSE-APACHE-2.0. The original LMA C++ controller/CLI are MIT licensed.

Upstream HiFT's Snake activation cites Edward Dixon's MIT implementation.
The pinned SoulX checkout references an incl_licenses directory that it does
not include. LICENSE-SNAKE-MIT preserves the actual EdwardDixon/snake MIT
notice from the independently pinned upstream repository; it is not a
reconstruction of that missing SoulX directory.

The controller uses separately pinned ONNX Runtime headers and links its
CPU runtime, MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.
The complete notice is LICENSE-ONNX-RUNTIME-MIT. The shared DSP library's
Apache-2.0 and KISS FFT BSD-3-Clause notices remain in research/soulx/.
The JSON CLI dependency is nlohmann/json, MIT, (c) 2013-2025 Niels Lohmann;
its existing repository notice is third_party/notices/sd-nlohmann-json-LICENSE.txt.

The original modules and optional export/test dependencies are downloaded
to ignored build directories. Full-network synthetic test parameters are
UNTRAINED fixtures, not publisher checkpoints or model-quality evidence.
No models, reference audio, tokenizers, acoustic exports, host DLLs, Python
packages or research binaries are added to the APK by this module.
